{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) &nbsp;A metric&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">d</span></span>&nbsp;on a set&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">X</span></span> must always satisfy:", "option1": "&nbsp;Linearity", "option2": "Triangle inequality", "option3": "Differentiability", "option4": "&nbsp;Continuity", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>One of the four defining properties of a metric is the <strong data-start=\"444\" data-end=\"467\">triangle inequality</strong>. Linearity, differentiability, and continuity are not required.</p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) The Cantor set is:", "option1": "Countable, closed, nowhere dense.", "option2": "Uncountable, closed, nowhere dense.", "option3": "Countable, open, dense.", "option4": "Uncountable, open, dense.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_piAmjjc.png\" width=\"360\" height=\"123\"></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which of the following is a perfect set in R?", "option1": "<span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span>", "option2": "<span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span>", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Q</span></span> (rationals)", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_gUJt3jk.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"493\" height=\"156\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_IkLNjW4.png\" width=\"520\" height=\"80\">", "option1": "Convergent → (1/2)", "option2": "Convergent → 1", "option3": "Convergent → 0", "option4": "Divergent", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_J3VcNap.png\" width=\"497\" height=\"105\"></p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which of the following is not a property of a metric?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-27_102353819.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"288\" height=\"41\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-27_102441876.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"262\" height=\"38\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-27_102525787.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"250\" height=\"45\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_DRR0sJn.png\" width=\"254\" height=\"33\">", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_wCDXhih.png\" width=\"767\" height=\"68\"></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_lAKI9aY.png\" width=\"483\" height=\"58\">", "option1": "Convergent → 3", "option2": "Convergent → 2", "option3": "Convergent → 1", "option4": "Divergent", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_tA2w4qF.png\" width=\"415\" height=\"73\"></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_wbfhgk6.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"443\" height=\"149\">", "option1": "Convergent → 0", "option2": "Convergent → 1", "option3": "Divergent", "option4": "Oscillating", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_TSlKIBS.png\" width=\"425\" height=\"59\"></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) In the discrete metric, the distance between two distinct points is:", "option1": "1", "option2": "0", "option3": "Infinity", "option4": "Undefined", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_konUNEK.png\" width=\"472\" height=\"45\"></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which of the following subsets of RR with usual Euclidean metric is compact?", "option1": "(0, 1)", "option2": "[0, 1]", "option3": "(- ∞, ∞)", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_6iN3QaU.png\" width=\"473\" height=\"46\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which of the following is Cauchy but not monotone?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_mFSLdRK.png\" width=\"138\" height=\"35\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_uXnwmmT.png\" width=\"220\" height=\"53\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_TpHmdK2.png\" width=\"158\" height=\"48\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_j4DnhBA.png\" width=\"199\" height=\"37\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_HzdwF1g.png\" width=\"469\" height=\"150\"></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_XgFt4yb.png\" width=\"548\" height=\"63\">", "option1": "Convergent → 2", "option2": "Convergent → 1", "option3": "Divergent", "option4": "Oscillating", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_pIYcGMX.png\" width=\"491\" height=\"108\"></p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which of the following functions on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">R</span></span> is a metric?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_f81LzHN.png\" width=\"291\" height=\"59\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_pPcFrJw.png\" width=\"302\" height=\"46\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_7t7xCSd.png\" width=\"302\" height=\"50\">", "option4": "Both A and C", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_bXrM6Vr.png\" width=\"678\" height=\"109\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_ddVnI4u.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"934\" height=\"78\">", "option1": "Euclidean metric", "option2": "Discrete metric", "option3": "Manhattan (Taxicab) metric", "option4": "Maximum metric", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-27_213019244.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"545\" height=\"46\"></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) True about every convergent sequence:", "option1": "Must be bounded", "option2": "Must be monotone", "option3": "Must be Cauchy", "option4": "Both A and C", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_JoyHV3O.png\" width=\"384\" height=\"92\"></p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_5l9OHUN.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"662\" height=\"111\">", "option1": "Yes, because it satisfies all four metric properties.", "option2": "No, because it violates symmetry.", "option3": "No, because it violates the triangle inequality.", "option4": "No, because&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">d(x,y)=0</span></span>&nbsp;does not imply&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x=y</span></span>.", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_FMVpl53.png\" width=\"497\" height=\"129\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_zuaP2AC.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"557\" height=\"90\"><br>Which is true?", "option1": "This is not a metric.", "option2": "This is a metric equivalent to the discrete metric.", "option3": "This is a metric but not equivalent to the discrete metric.", "option4": "This is a metric only for finite sets.", "answer": "0", "exp": "<p data-start=\"1706\" data-end=\"1941\">This is just a <strong data-start=\"1742\" data-end=\"1783\">scaled version of the discrete metric</strong> (using 2 instead of 1). Scaling by a positive constant preserves metric properties and yields the same topology, so it’s equivalent to the discrete metric.</p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_Cs2V0tV.png\" width=\"568\" height=\"64\">", "option1": "Convergent", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_FkpxTwd.png\" width=\"82\" height=\"28\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_Kn6flpN.png\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\">", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_GqWGAmW.png\" width=\"354\" height=\"37\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip6_lqShb46.png\" width=\"75\" height=\"24\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_0jCf5BD.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"537\" height=\"218\"><br>Which is correct?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_ah6TvBj.png\" width=\"406\" height=\"44\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_ZnxPAun.png\" width=\"734\" height=\"38\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_w1kZwEo.png\" width=\"277\" height=\"48\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip6.png\" width=\"407\" height=\"42\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip7.png\" width=\"691\" height=\"108\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Let (X,d) be a metric space. Which of the following statements is always true?", "option1": "Every convergent sequence is Cauchy.", "option2": "Every Cauchy sequence converges.", "option3": "Every bounded sequence is Cauchy.", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-27_222030412.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"445\" height=\"76\"></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which of the following metric spaces is not complete?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_nJoZEMd.png\" width=\"338\" height=\"52\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_IAVonvv.png\" width=\"322\" height=\"56\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_FCZm3K8.png\" width=\"295\" height=\"46\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_zMfjmw2.png\" width=\"275\" height=\"45\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_NvRjYGT.png\" width=\"690\" height=\"114\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_hFUM1Xt.png\" width=\"643\" height=\"51\">", "option1": "(0,1)", "option2": "[0,1)", "option3": "[0, 1]", "option4": "(- ∞, ∞)", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_WRDeTZK.png\" width=\"597\" height=\"163\"></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which of the following properties are true for the standard&nbsp;Cantor set&nbsp;C ⊂ [0,1]?", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">C</span></span></span></span> is uncountable", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">C</span></span> has Lebesgue measure zero.", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">C</span></span></span></span> is closed and perfect.", "option4": "All of These", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_scch7cY.png\" width=\"492\" height=\"110\"></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Which of the following is&nbsp;not a Cauchy sequence?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_5kfjGjG.png\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_RUZ553D.png\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_FPZunFF.png\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_MbvEk70.png\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_6CZqAFE.png\" width=\"547\" height=\"55\"></p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) True statement about Cauchy sequences in R", "option1": "Every Cauchy sequence diverges", "option2": "Every Cauchy sequence converges", "option3": "Only bounded Cauchy sequences converge", "option4": "Only monotone Cauchy sequences converge", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_5WYaDJ2.png\" width=\"470\" height=\"84\"></p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) A&nbsp;perfect set in a metric space is:", "option1": "A closed set with no isolated points.", "option2": "A set where every point is a limit point.", "option3": "&nbsp;A compact set.", "option4": "Both A and B.", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_hiaE4Gz.png\" width=\"409\" height=\"104\"></p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which of the following are true?", "option1": "Every compact metric space is complete.", "option2": "Every complete and totally bounded metric space is compact.", "option3": "Every closed subset of a compact metric space is compact.", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_3lYkQn3.png\" width=\"598\" height=\"83\"></p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which of the following sequences is&nbsp;Cauchy in&nbsp;<span aria-hidden=\"true\">Q</span>&nbsp;but does&nbsp;not converge in&nbsp;<span aria-hidden=\"true\">Q</span>?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_avt3s8X.png\" width=\"131\" height=\"57\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_00eL9ej.png\" width=\"181\" height=\"54\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_iTr4u9Z.png\" width=\"758\" height=\"40\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_FNJwFLj.png\" width=\"174\" height=\"37\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_Lblb3DN.png\" width=\"831\" height=\"58\"></p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which sequence is Cauchy?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_nCduVg1.png\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_xeR5jnn.png\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_1wyKuwX.png\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_EQHK1Ca.png\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_lcFjk3Z.png\" width=\"467\" height=\"92\"></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Evaluate the limit:<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_6NFZCbm.png\" width=\"268\" height=\"138\">", "option1": "1/2", "option2": "3/5", "option3": "0", "option4": "∞", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/image_2025-08-28_011247650.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"419\" height=\"115\"></p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) A&nbsp;metric space is a pair:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_xOOcHWr.png\" width=\"85\" height=\"36\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_R212pTG.png\" width=\"471\" height=\"31\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_AO6j928.png\" width=\"117\" height=\"40\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_E9YuCwE.png\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>A metric space is defined as a set <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">X</span></span> with a <strong data-start=\"459\" data-end=\"475\">metric <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">d</span></span></strong> that measures distance between elements.</p>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_OtT9YZH.png\" width=\"497\" height=\"45\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "∞", "option4": "Does not Exist", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_RMJgmuR.png\"></p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which of the following metric spaces is&nbsp;bounded?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_ZzmdnEY.png\" width=\"259\" height=\"44\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_mODb7uL.png\" width=\"316\" height=\"45\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_CFyQOIz.png\" width=\"275\" height=\"42\">", "option4": "All of These", "answer": "2", "exp": "<ul data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1914\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1853\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1798\" data-end=\"1853\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">R,N </span></span>are unbounded.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1854\" data-end=\"1914\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1856\" data-end=\"1914\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[0,1]</span></span> is bounded since all distances are <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">≤1</span></span>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Which condition ensures that&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">d(x,y) = 0</span></span>&nbsp;only when&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x = y</span></span>?", "option1": "&nbsp;Non-negativity", "option2": "&nbsp;Symmetry", "option3": "Identity of indiscernibles", "option4": "Triangle inequality", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Identity of indiscernibles means <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">d(x, y)=0  ⟺  x=y</span></span>.</p>"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_i8ESdFv.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"656\" height=\"70\">", "option1": "Euclidean metric", "option2": "Manhattan metric", "option3": "Chebyshev metric", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>This is the <strong data-start=\"2282\" data-end=\"2300\">maximum (Chebyshev) metric</strong>.</p>"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Every Cauchy sequence in a&nbsp;complete metric space:", "option1": "Diverges", "option2": "Is bounded but not convergent", "option3": "Converges to some point in the space", "option4": "Is eventually constant", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p> Completeness = all Cauchy sequences converge in the space.</p>"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_02g4RQ1.png\" width=\"414\" height=\"69\">", "option1": "Increasing", "option2": "Decreasing", "option3": "Oscillating", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p> Each term is smaller than the previous → decreasing.</p>"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_vdrzbVi.png\" width=\"224\" height=\"73\">", "option1": "Bounded", "option2": "Unbounded", "option3": "Convergent", "option4": "Constant", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Exponentially increasing → goes to infinity → unbounded.</p>"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_vGA5Fsm.png\" width=\"470\" height=\"75\">", "option1": "Convergent", "option2": "Divergent", "option3": "&nbsp;Increasing", "option4": "Constant", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_o717EXS.png\" width=\"597\" height=\"113\"></p>"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_kn3lWxD.png\" width=\"531\" height=\"55\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "∞", "option4": "Doesn not Converse", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><strong><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_37InG0r.png\" width=\"446\" height=\"95\"></strong></p>"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Every bounded monotonic sequence:", "option1": "Diverges", "option2": "Converges", "option3": "Oscillates", "option4": "Is constant", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_EgaorxC.png\" width=\"490\" height=\"138\"></p>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 12099, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "2700000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "3000000", "examname": "Aug 30, 2025", "type": "Math-Sub-561-applied", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}